+
+# The sweep is asserted by execution against pinned sentences before it is used, because the two ways
+# it can be wrong cost different things and both have shipped. Missing a real figure is the hole it was
+# added to close. Firing on correct prose is worse: this gate blocks CI, so a sweep that accuses the
+# skill's own rule sentences is a sweep somebody turns off, and then the first fault is uncovered too.
+#
+# The sweep is ONE invocation, and this is the whole of it. The fixture table below and the live check
+# at the bottom of this block both call it, so the table pins the flag list as well as the pattern.
+# Written out twice instead — `grep -qiE "$STAT"` in the table and `grep -rqiE "$STAT"
+# three-loop-workflow/` live — the table would pin `$STAT`, which is not the sweep: dropping `-i` from
+# the live copy alone leaves every case green while `Seventy findings came back from the second
+# reviewer.` ships. `-H` so the line-number prefix is present whichever grep is on PATH; the fixture
+# reader below needs it and the live listing wants it.
+stat_scan() { grep -rniHE "$STAT" "$@"; }
