+# RULENUM is out of the findings arm, so its tokens are pinned where they still decide something.
+for _w in zero one two three; do sweep_case catches "a $_w percent uplift"; done
+sweep_case catches 'Sixty of the ninety confirmed findings were defects'
+# The two arms nothing above depends on. Without these two cases both could be deleted with every other
+# case still green, and `pinned by execution` would be a claim this table does not keep.
+sweep_case catches 'the second reviewer found 56.5% of the defects'
+# No numeral, deliberately: `30-70 percentage points` would be caught by the arm above it on `70
+# percent`, leaving this literal still unpinned. Bare, it is the only thing that can match.
+sweep_case catches 'the gap between reviewers is measured in percentage points'
+# Ordinary prose in this skill's own register. The first four are rule sentences shipped today or one
+# innocuous reword away from them: build.md:38 clears the un-anchored version by a single character.
+sweep_case admits  '**Standard: one reviewer. Deep: two, in parallel, independent — union their findings.**'
+sweep_case admits  '**Standard: one reviewer. Deep: two, in parallel: union their findings.**'
+sweep_case admits  '**Standard: one reviewer. Deep: two in parallel, union their findings.**'
+sweep_case admits  'Take the union of their findings'
+sweep_case admits  'None of the blocking findings survived triage this round.'
+sweep_case admits  'Once the reviewer is done, triage the reported findings.'
+sweep_case admits  'a milestone reached before the reviewer reports findings'
+sweep_case admits  'Someone reviewing a diff returns findings'
